        setup: {
          players: 'Four players in fixed partnerships (partners opposite). Deal and play counter-clockwise. Two-player variant exists.',
          deck: 'Standard 52-card pack, no jokers. English pattern.',
          equipment: 'Standard 52-card deck, score sheet (optional), table space.',
          dealing: 'Dealer gives 4 cards to player on right and 4 face down on table. That player bids (9–13) and plays one card from the four; dealer then deals the rest in groups of four counter-clockwise. Bidder ends with 11 cards, others 12.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Capture cards worth points from the layout (floor). The game ends when one team has a lead of at least 100 points over the other (a baazi). Capture by playing a card that matches the capture value of one or more cards or houses on the table; build houses (piles that can only be captured as a unit) to protect or consolidate captures.',
          gameplay: 'Deal: First dealer random; dealer gives 4 cards to player on right and 4 face down on table. That player bids 9–13 (capture value) if possible, then must create a house of that value, pick up cards of that value, or throw the bid card as loose. Dealer then deals remainder in fours counter-clockwise (bidder has 11 cards, others 12). Play proceeds counter-clockwise. Each turn: play one card to (1) create or add to a house, (2) pick up matching cards or houses, or (3) throw a loose card. Houses are piles of 9–13 capture value; ordinary houses can be broken or cemented; cemented houses cannot be broken. Must pick up all cards that match the played card. Sweep (taking all floor cards) scores 50 (25 on first play, 0 on last). Last picker takes any remaining loose cards.',
          keyRules: [
            'Capture value: A=1, 2–10 face, J=11, Q=12, K=13',
            'Only spades (1–13), aces of other suits (1 each), and 10♦ (6) score; total 100 points',
            'First team to lead by 100 wins one baazi; team scoring under 9 in a deal loses a baazi immediately',
            'House owner must hold a card matching house value until captured or broken',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Remember cards left in denominations 9–K and point-carrying cards picked up. Try to leave only two items on the floor when possible.',
          intermediate: 'Ensure your side is last to pick up so you take remaining loose cards at end. Cement houses you want to keep; pick up with point cards if you fear the house will be broken or taken.',
          advanced: 'If you and partner hold all four of a denomination, build a cemented house in that value; opponents cannot break or capture it. Use house ownership and card memory to force favourable end-game.',
          tips: [
            'Leave two items totalling at least 14 when possible to reduce sweep risk',
            'Dealer can delay picking up a cemented house until last turn to keep loose cards for your team',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
